// UAP — keep the X server and xrdp stack out of automatic (unattended) upgrades.
//
// An RDP desktop is an Xorg process in a logind scope (session-cN.scope). If
// unattended-upgrades swaps xserver-xorg-core / xrdp under a LIVE session, the
// stack is restarted, the running desktop is orphaned, and the next reconnect
// builds a fresh blank desktop (you "lose" your session; orphans pile up).
//
// These packages can't be live-swapped under a session — apply them yourself at
// a reboot:  sudo apt update && sudo apt install xserver-xorg-core xorgxrdp xrdp && sudo reboot
// Everything else still auto-patches normally.
Unattended-Upgrade::Package-Blacklist {
    "xserver-xorg-core";
    "xserver-common";
    "xserver-xorg-legacy";
    "xorgxrdp";
    "xrdp";
};
